 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "To say what you do",
   "texto": [
    "Hva jobber du med? is used to ask «What do you do?». Although it literally means «What are you working with?», it does not translate word for word.",
    "To say «work as», jobber som is used: Jeg jobber som lærer. With er or jobber som, the name of the profession usually goes without article: Jeg er lærer, not «jeg er en lærer» in this basic presentation.",
    "Studerer means «study». Like the other verbs in the present, it maintains the same shape with jeg and du."
   ]
  },
